<header class="page-hero wrap">
  <span class="eyebrow">Experience Lead · Service Design → Launch → Optimization · Merkle (dentsu)</span>
  <h1>HEMS <span class="em">eCommerce</span></h1>
</header>

<article class="case case--brief" id="hems-gate-target">
  <div class="jmap brief-keep">
    <div class="dev-stage">
      <div class="dev-lap"><div class="view"><img src="/assets/img/hems/live-home-desktop.jpg" alt="The live gmenergy.com homepage scrolling on a MacBook Pro"></div><img class="bezel" src="/assets/img/hems/bezel-mbp14.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="dev-ph"><div class="view"><img src="/assets/img/hems/live-hes-mobile.jpg" alt="Home Energy System product page scrolling on an iPhone"></div><img class="bezel" src="/assets/img/hems/bezel-iphone16pro.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="brief-keep" style="display:flex;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:6px">
    <div class="view-toggle" role="tablist" aria-label="Case study view">
      <button class="vt-btn on" id="vt-brief" type="button" aria-selected="true">Brief</button>
      <button class="vt-btn" id="vt-full" type="button" aria-selected="false">Full</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="case-gate brief-keep" id="hems-gate">
    <div class="gate-title">The full case study is password protected</div>
    <div class="gate-sub">It includes sensitive images and workflows. Enter the password to view it.</div>
    <input id="hems-pw" type="password" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Password" />
    <div class="gate-err" id="hems-err"></div>
    <button id="hems-go" type="button">View full case study</button>
  </div>
  <p class="notice"><b>Note</b>Due to the sensitive nature of this work, some images are blurred or omitted — only publicly available visuals are shown.</p>
  <div class="brief-keep" style="max-width:820px;margin:26px auto 0">
    <h2 style="padding-top:0">Overview</h2>
    <p>GM Energy's first step into ecommerce — taking their home energy management system (HEMS) line from no digital presence to a launched, financed, installable commerce experience, and building the research practice that keeps improving it.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="case-meta brief-keep">
    <div><span>Role</span>User Experience Lead</div>
    <div><span>Client</span>GM Energy · via Merkle (dentsu)</div>
    <div><span>Timeline</span>Oct 2022 – 2026 · vision through post-launch optimization</div>
    <div><span>Team</span>Rotating core team of 6–10</div>
  </div>


  <div class="impact-block brief-keep">
    <h2>Impact</h2>
    <ul class="impact-list">
      <li><b>Took GM Energy from zero to a launched commerce experience</b><span>Defined what the experience should be — service blueprint, personas, journeys — then carried it through wireframes, sprint delivery, and launch: configurable bundles, financing inside checkout, installation scheduling, and account management.</span></li>
      <li><b>Unified purchase, financing, and installation into one checkout</b><span>Took what began as a hand-off between GM Energy, GM Financial, and the install partner and integrated it into a single flow — purchasing the products, financing them with installation, and quoting the install in one process, so the customer is never passed back and forth. One of the hardest problems in the project, and it took many iterations to get right.</span></li>
      <li><b>Established the research framework for validation testing</b><span>Set the foundation for how the team tests: every study starts by defining what we're asking, why we're asking it, what the result should tell us — and how that answer will drive the design decision. Our senior UX designer then evolved that foundation into the mature, well-defined testing process the team runs today.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat"><b>0 → 1</b><span>No digital presence to a launched, financed, installable storefront</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>4 personas</b><span>Evidence-based, reshaping who the business designs for</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>7+ workstreams</b><span>Storefront · Checkout · Sales guide · Installation · Energy Genie · Executive dashboard · Dealership experience</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="brief-keep">
    <h2>The major tracks</h2>
    <p>One engagement, many parallel workstreams — moved between continuously from 2022 through launch and beyond.</p>
    <div class="track-cards">
      <div class="tcard"><div class="shot"><img src="/assets/img/hems/live-home-desktop.jpg" alt="The live GM Energy homepage" loading="lazy"></div><b>Storefront</b><span>Wireframed the full site, went deep on home, landing, and product pages, then handed off to the UI team to apply visual design. Hover to scroll the live homepage.</span></div>
      <div class="tcard"><div class="shot"><img src="/assets/img/hems/fig-checkout-review.jpg" alt="Checkout review step — final design" loading="lazy"></div><b>Checkout &amp; financing</b><span>Unified purchase, GM Financial financing, and install quoting into one flow — the customer is never passed between three companies.</span></div>
      <div class="tcard"><div class="shot"><img src="/assets/img/hems/fig-chart-quote-eligibility.jpg" alt="Install quote eligibility step" loading="lazy"></div><b>Installation questionnaire</b><span>The step-by-step home assessment that turns an installation into a quote inside checkout.</span></div>
